1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,698
Meet Management Agent, a classifier for condominium resident requests.

2
00:00:05,878 --> 00:00:11,055
It turns a message into a category, priority, and suggested team.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:19,864
A resident reports a flickering corridor light. Staff enter the message and, optionally, its location.

4
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:26,084
The classifier identifies maintenance and suggests the maintenance team.

5
00:00:26,264 --> 00:00:31,527
The model score stays visible, and uncertain requests are flagged for review.

6
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:37,632
A child trapped in a lift triggers an emergency flag before any model call.

7
00:00:37,812 --> 00:00:42,172
The app prompts human action; it does not dispatch help.

8
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:50,141
Staff can upload a CSV inbox, inspect the classifications, and export the results.

9
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:53,365
No tickets are created automatically.

10
00:00:54,533 --> 00:01:00,689
The starter workflow classified fifty three of fifty five synthetic examples correctly.

11
00:01:00,869 --> 00:01:05,193
This is a development check, not real resident accuracy.

12
00:01:06,325 --> 00:01:12,861
The offline demo is ready. The Ollama adapter still needs live model evaluation.

13
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:17,962
Next: label real resident requests and calibrate the classifier.
